        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "problemStatement": "Create a `UserCredential` class with `private String username` and `private String passwordHash`. In security, sensitive credentials should be write-only: do NOT provide `getPasswordHash()`. Instead, provide `setPassword(String currentPassword, String newPassword)` returning boolean. It must verify `currentPassword` matches internal password before updating, and require `newPassword` to be at least 8 characters long. Provide `authenticate(String attempt)` returning boolean. In `main()`, initialize user 'alice' with password 'Secret123', fail an update with a 4-letter password 'test', successfully update to 'NewSecurePass2026', and authenticate.",
        "hint": "Never expose a getter for password or passwordHash; verify credentials internally with authenticate().",
        "solutionCode": "public class Solution {\n    static class UserCredential {\n        private String username;\n        private String passwordHash;\n\n        public UserCredential(String username, String initialPassword) {\n            this.username = username;\n            this.passwordHash = \"HASH_\" + initialPassword;\n        }\n\n        public String getUsername() { return username; }\n\n        public boolean authenticate(String attempt) {\n            return this.passwordHash.equals(\"HASH_\" + attempt);\n        }\n\n        public boolean setPassword(String currentPassword, String newPassword) {\n            if (!authenticate(currentPassword)) {\n                return false;\n            }\n            if (newPassword == null || newPassword.length() < 8) {\n                return false;\n            }\n            this.passwordHash = \"HASH_\" + newPassword;\n            return true;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        UserCredential user = new UserCredential(\"alice\", \"Secret123\");\n        System.out.println(\"Auth Secret123: \" + user.authenticate(\"Secret123\"));\n\n        boolean shortUpdate = user.setPassword(\"Secret123\", \"test\");\n        System.out.println(\"Update with short pass: \" + shortUpdate);\n\n        boolean validUpdate = user.setPassword(\"Secret123\", \"NewSecurePass2026\");\n        System.out.println(\"Update with strong pass: \" + validUpdate);\n        System.out.println(\"Auth with new pass: \" + user.authenticate(\"NewSecurePass2026\"));\n    }\n}",
        "output": "Auth Secret123: true\nUpdate with short pass: false\nUpdate with strong pass: true\nAuth with new pass: true",
        "explanation": "Omitting getters for sensitive state (write-only encapsulation) protects secrets from accidental logging, serialization leaks, or unauthorized reads."
